{"name":"El Paso","hex":"#39392c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"El Paso","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city, the county seat of El Paso County, Texas, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/El_Paso"}],"entries":[{"title":"El Paso (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"El Paso\" is a western ballad written and originally recorded by Marty Robbins, and first released on Gunfighter Ballads and Trail Songs in September 1959. It was released as a single the following month, and became a major hit on both the country and pop music charts, becoming the first No. 1 hit of the 1960s on both. It won the Grammy Award for Best Country & Western Recording in 1961. It is widely considered a genre classic for its gripping narrative which ends in the death of its protagonist, its shift from past to present tense, haunting harmonies by vocalists Bobby Sykes and Jim Glaser and the eloquent and varied Spanish guitar accompaniment by Grady Martin that lends the recording a distinctive Tex-Mex feel. The name of the character Feleena was based upon a schoolmate of Robbins in the fifth grade, Fidelina Martinez."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a6/El_Paso_by_Marty_Robbins_single_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Paso_(song)"},{"title":"El Paso, Texas","blocks":[{"text":"El Paso is a city in and the county seat of El Paso County, Texas, United States. It is the 23rd-most populous city in the U.S., sixth-most populous city in Texas, and the most populous city in West Texas with a population of 678,815 at the 2020 census. The El Paso metropolitan area has an estimated 879,000 residents."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/El_Paso_Cityscape_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-El_Paso_Cityscape_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Paso%2C_Texas"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Southwest_University_Park.jpg/500px-Southwest_University_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Southwest_University_Park.jpg/500px-Southwest_University_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASouthwest_University_Park.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/YsletaMission.JPG/500px-YsletaMission.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/YsletaMission.JPG/1280px-YsletaMission.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/YsletaMission.JPG/500px-YsletaMission.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYsletaMission.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/UTEP5.JPG/500px-UTEP5.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/UTEP5.JPG/1280px-UTEP5.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/UTEP5.JPG/500px-UTEP5.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUTEP5.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Summitanthonysnose1b.jpg/500px-Summitanthonysnose1b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Summitanthonysnose1b.jpg/5